window.EASTERTIDE = {"days": [{"day": 1, "date": "2027-04-11", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "The gate and the voice", "ref": "John 10:1-10", "leadIn": "Jesus describes a shepherd whose sheep know his voice and follow him. He calls himself the gate and says he came so that his sheep might have life, and have it abundantly.", "prayer": "Good Shepherd, there are many voices pulling at me: news, worry, other people's opinions. Help me to know your voice among them. Open the gate for me, and lead me out to pasture and to the full life you promise. Amen.", "reflect": "Which voices pull the loudest on you? What does Jesus's voice sound like next to them?"}, {"day": 2, "date": "2027-04-12", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "The good shepherd", "ref": "John 10:11-18", "leadIn": "A hired hand runs when the wolf comes, but the good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep. Jesus says no one takes his life from him: he lays it down, and he has power to take it up again.", "prayer": "Jesus, you gave your life for me, and you live. Thank you for knowing me by name, and for staying when others run. Keep me close to you today, and help me trust your care when I feel like one more face in the crowd. Amen.", "reflect": "What does it mean to you that the shepherd knows you personally?"}, {"day": 3, "date": "2027-04-13", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "No one will snatch them", "ref": "John 10:22-30", "leadIn": "Some demand a plain answer about who Jesus is. He points to his works and to the sheep who hear him. He promises eternal life to those who follow, and says no one can snatch them out of his hand.", "prayer": "Lord, I rest in your hand. When I feel unsure of my faith, my future, or myself, remind me that I am held by you, and no one can take me from you. Let that settle me, and make me gentle with other people. Amen.", "reflect": "When do you most need to hear that you are held and cannot be lost?"}, {"day": 4, "date": "2027-04-14", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "I myself will search", "ref": "Ezekiel 34:11-16", "leadIn": "God speaks through Ezekiel against shepherds who neglect the flock. Then he promises to be the shepherd himself: to search for the lost, bring back the strayed, bind up the injured, and strengthen the weak.", "prayer": "God my shepherd, find me when I wander. Bring me back from the places I scattered to. Bind up what is broken in me and strengthen what is weak. Let me rest in your care today, and trust that you are still looking for me. Amen.", "reflect": "Which part do you most need today: being found, bound up, or strengthened?"}, {"day": 5, "date": "2027-04-15", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "By his wounds", "ref": "1 Peter 2:19-25", "leadIn": "Peter holds up Christ as the example for people who suffer unjustly. He bore our sins in his body, and by his wounds we are healed. We were like sheep going astray, but have now returned to the shepherd and guardian of our souls.", "prayer": "Lord Jesus, you carried what I could not carry, and by your wounds I am healed. Thank you for bringing me home when I was going astray. Help me follow your example, and give me wisdom and courage when I am wronged or treated unfairly. Amen.", "reflect": "Where do you need healing, and where do you need to return?"}, {"day": 6, "date": "2027-04-16", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "Come, let us worship", "ref": "Psalm 95:1-7", "leadIn": "The psalmist calls God's people to sing, to kneel, and to give thanks. The reason given is simple: the Lord is our God, and we are the people of his pasture and the sheep in his hand.", "prayer": "Lord, you are my God and I am your sheep. I come before you with thanks and worship this morning, and leave my worries at the door. You made me, and I am in your care. Let me sing, even quietly. Amen.", "reflect": "What are three things you can thank God for right now?"}, {"day": 7, "date": "2027-04-17", "week": "Week 3: The Good Shepherd", "title": "A great multitude", "ref": "Revelation 7:9-17", "leadIn": "John sees a crowd too large to count, from every nation, standing before the throne and the Lamb. The Lamb is their shepherd, and God wipes every tear from their eyes. It is the end of the Good Shepherd's story.", "prayer": "Lamb of God, thank you that the day is coming when there will be no hunger, no thirst, and no tears. Until then, hold me, and hold the ones I love. Make me more aware of people who are hungry and grieving now. Amen.", "reflect": "How does this picture of the future change how you face today?"}, {"day": 8, "date": "2027-04-18", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "The vine and the branches", "ref": "John 15:1-8", "leadIn": "Jesus calls himself the true vine and his followers the branches. A branch cannot bear fruit by itself. It has to stay connected, so he says: abide in me, and I in you.", "prayer": "Jesus, keep me connected to you, because on my own I wither. Where you need to prune, do it gently. Let the life that flows from you show up in what I do and say, and let my work bear fruit that lasts. Amen.", "reflect": "What helps you stay connected to Christ? What pulls you away?"}, {"day": 9, "date": "2027-04-19", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "Love one another", "ref": "John 15:9-17", "leadIn": "Jesus tells his disciples to remain in his love, and to love one another as he has loved them. He no longer calls them servants but friends, and says he chose them to go and bear fruit.", "prayer": "Lord, you called me a friend, not a servant, and you chose me. Help me to love the people near me the way you have loved me, including the ones who are difficult. Let your joy be in me, and let it be complete. Amen.", "reflect": "Who is one person you can love in a practical way today?"}, {"day": 10, "date": "2027-04-20", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "Let not your heart be troubled", "ref": "John 14:1-7", "leadIn": "On the night before his death, Jesus comforts his friends. He is going to prepare a place for them, and he says he is the way, the truth, and the life.", "prayer": "Jesus, calm my troubled heart. You say there are many rooms in your Father's house and you are preparing a place. I trust you to lead me. When I do not know the way, remind me that you are the way. Amen.", "reflect": "What is troubling your heart? Can you hand it over to him now?"}, {"day": 11, "date": "2027-04-21", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "I will not leave you orphaned", "ref": "John 14:15-21", "leadIn": "Jesus promises another Helper, the Spirit of truth, who will be with his followers forever. He says he will not leave them as orphans, and that those who love him will be loved by his Father.", "prayer": "Lord, thank you that I am not alone and that you did not leave me orphaned. Send your Spirit of truth to be with me. Let me know your presence today, in ordinary moments, and help me keep your commands out of love. Amen.", "reflect": "When have you most clearly felt you were not alone?"}, {"day": 12, "date": "2027-04-22", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "Love in truth and action", "ref": "1 John 3:16-24", "leadIn": "John says we know love because Christ laid down his life for us, so we should do the same for one another. Love shows up in action and truth, not only in words.", "prayer": "God, make my love real and not only words. Show me one need I can meet today, and give me the courage and the means to meet it. When my heart condemns me, remind me that you are greater than my heart. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one concrete act of love you could do this week?"}, {"day": 13, "date": "2027-04-23", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "Seek the Lord", "ref": "Isaiah 55:6-13", "leadIn": "Isaiah invites people to seek the Lord while he can be found. God's thoughts are higher than ours, and his word goes out like rain, accomplishing what he sends it to do. The mountains break into singing.", "prayer": "Lord, your ways are higher than mine, and your thoughts are not my thoughts. Let your word do its work in me today the way rain waters the earth. Help me seek you while you are near, and return to you. Amen.", "reflect": "How has God's word surprised you or grown something in you?"}, {"day": 14, "date": "2027-04-24", "week": "Week 4: Abiding", "title": "Like a tree by the water", "ref": "Psalm 1", "leadIn": "The first psalm describes a person who delights in God's word. They are like a tree planted by streams, bearing fruit in season. It is a picture of what abiding looks like over a lifetime.", "prayer": "Lord, plant me by living water. Let my roots go deep in your word, so that I do not wither when the heat comes. Teach me to delight in your way, to keep company with the wise, and to bear fruit in season. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one small habit that would help your roots go deeper?"}, {"day": 15, "date": "2027-04-25", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "Rise and walk", "ref": "Acts 3:1-10", "leadIn": "On the way to the temple, Peter and John meet a man who has been unable to walk all his life. Peter gives him no money but takes him by the hand in the name of Jesus, and he stands up, leaping and praising God.", "prayer": "Risen Lord, you still lift people up. At the gate, a man who could not walk was made whole in the name of Jesus. Use my hands for your work today, and help me really look at someone I usually pass by. Amen.", "reflect": "Who is someone near you that needs a hand more than money?"}, {"day": 16, "date": "2027-04-26", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "One heart and soul", "ref": "Acts 4:32-35", "leadIn": "The first believers shared everything and no one among them was in need. The resurrection shaped how they lived together: generously, and with great power in their witness.", "prayer": "God, make my life open-handed. The early church had everything in common, and no one was in need. Show me what I can share, and with whom. Free me from clutching what I have, and bind your people together. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one thing you could give or share that would meet a real need?"}, {"day": 17, "date": "2027-04-27", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "Brother Saul", "ref": "Acts 9:10-19", "leadIn": "Ananias is afraid to visit Saul, who had persecuted the church. God tells him to go anyway. Ananias lays hands on Saul and calls him brother, and Saul is given sight and is baptized.", "prayer": "Lord, give me the courage of Ananias. He was afraid, and he went anyway. Help me to welcome the people you are changing, even when I remember who they used to be. Let me say \"brother\" or \"sister\" and mean it. Amen.", "reflect": "Is there someone you find hard to see as a brother or sister? What might God be doing in them?"}, {"day": 18, "date": "2027-04-28", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "God shows no favoritism", "ref": "Acts 10:34-43", "leadIn": "Peter visits a Roman household and says he now sees that God accepts people from every nation. He tells the story of Jesus: his ministry, his death, and his resurrection, and that forgiveness comes through his name.", "prayer": "Lord, your welcome is wider than I expect. Peter learned that you show no favoritism, and I need to learn it again. Make my heart as wide as yours. Show me who I have left outside, and give me the nerve to open the door. Amen.", "reflect": "Where might you be drawing a line that God is not?"}, {"day": 19, "date": "2027-04-29", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "What we have seen and heard", "ref": "1 John 1:1-4", "leadIn": "John writes about what he heard, saw, and touched: the word of life. He shares it so that others can have fellowship with him, and so that their joy may be complete.", "prayer": "God, let me speak of you from my own experience, from what I have seen and heard and known of you. Give me words that are honest and simple. Draw me closer to others who follow you, and let our joy be complete. Amen.", "reflect": "What has been your own experience of Jesus that you could share?"}, {"day": 20, "date": "2027-04-30", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "A feast for all", "ref": "Isaiah 25:6-9", "leadIn": "Isaiah pictures a feast God prepares for all peoples on the mountain. He will swallow up death forever and wipe away tears. On that day people will say, this is the Lord, we have waited for him.", "prayer": "Lord, I look forward to your feast, where you will wipe every tear and take away disgrace. Until then, help me trust you with what grieves me. Let me be glad even now, and say: this is the Lord, we trusted in him. Amen.", "reflect": "What grief do you carry that you want God to wipe away?"}, {"day": 21, "date": "2027-05-01", "week": "Week 5: Easter people", "title": "Making all things new", "ref": "Revelation 21:1-7", "leadIn": "John sees a new heaven and a new earth. God makes his home with his people, wipes away every tear, and says, I am making everything new. It is the final answer to Easter.", "prayer": "God, you make all things new, and you promised to wipe away every tear. Begin that work in me today, in the places that feel old and tired. Thank you that you are the beginning and the end, and that I am your child. Amen.", "reflect": "What is one thing in your life you hope God will make new?"}, {"day": 22, "date": "2027-05-02", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "The Spirit of truth", "ref": "John 16:5-15", "leadIn": "Jesus tells his friends it is better that he goes, because then the Helper will come. The Spirit will guide them into all truth and take what is Jesus's and make it known to them.", "prayer": "Holy Spirit, guide me into truth today, and help me hear what I cannot yet bear to hear. Make Christ known to me. Where I am confused or stubborn, be patient, and keep me from fooling myself. Amen.", "reflect": "Where do you need guidance right now?"}, {"day": 23, "date": "2027-05-03", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "Sorrow into joy", "ref": "John 16:16-24", "leadIn": "Jesus uses the picture of a woman in labor: pain, then joy at the birth. His friends will grieve, but he promises to see them again, and no one will take their joy away.", "prayer": "Lord, turn my sorrow into joy in your time. I do not like the waiting, but I trust that you are not done. Teach me to wait with hope, and to hold on to your promise that no one can take your joy from me. Amen.", "reflect": "What sorrow of yours do you want to hand over to him?"}, {"day": 24, "date": "2027-05-04", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "Eternal life", "ref": "John 17:1-11", "leadIn": "Jesus prays for himself and for his disciples. He says that eternal life is knowing the Father and the Son. He asks that the Father keep those who are his.", "prayer": "Father, eternal life is knowing you, so I want to know you. Not only to know about you, but to be known. Keep me in your name, and let your glory be seen in the ordinary ways I live today. Amen.", "reflect": "What would it mean to know God, and not only know about him?"}, {"day": 25, "date": "2027-05-05", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "That they may be one", "ref": "John 17:20-26", "leadIn": "Jesus prays for everyone who would believe through his disciples' word, which includes us. He asks that they all may be one, so that the world may believe. He wants them to share in the love the Father has for him.", "prayer": "Lord, make your people one. Start with me, in the relationships I find hard and the people I would rather avoid. Heal what is divided in your church and in my home, so that the world may see your love through us. Amen.", "reflect": "Where is there division you could help heal?"}, {"day": 26, "date": "2027-05-06", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "Ascension Day", "ref": "Acts 1:1-11", "leadIn": "After forty days of appearing to his friends, Jesus is taken up into heaven. He promises that they will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes, and be his witnesses. Two men in white clothing say he will come back in the same way.", "prayer": "Risen and ascended Lord, you reign over all, and you are not far away. Give me the power to be your witness where I am. Help me stop staring at the sky and get on with the work you have given me. Amen.", "reflect": "Where are you being called to be a witness this week?"}, {"day": 27, "date": "2027-05-07", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "Prayer for understanding", "ref": "Ephesians 1:15-23", "leadIn": "Paul prays that his readers would have eyes of the heart that are enlightened. He wants them to know the hope of their calling and the greatness of God's power, which raised Christ and set him above all things.", "prayer": "Father, open the eyes of my heart. Let me know the hope you have given me and the riches of your inheritance. Thank you for the power that raised Christ, and let me trust that same power is working for those who believe. Amen.", "reflect": "What would you like God to help you see more clearly?"}, {"day": 28, "date": "2027-05-08", "week": "Week 6: The promise of the Spirit", "title": "Clothed with power", "ref": "Luke 24:44-53", "leadIn": "Jesus opens his disciples' minds to understand the scriptures and tells them to wait in the city until they are clothed with power from on high. He blesses them and is carried up, and they return with great joy.", "prayer": "Lord, bless me as you blessed your friends on the hill. Fill me with joy, and send me. Open my mind to understand the scriptures, and help me wait for the power you promised. Let me return to worship with a glad heart. Amen.", "reflect": "What are you waiting for? How can you wait with joy?"}, {"day": 29, "date": "2027-05-09", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "Constant in prayer", "ref": "Acts 1:12-14", "leadIn": "After the ascension the disciples return to Jerusalem and gather in an upper room. They are together, with Mary and others, and they devote themselves to prayer.", "prayer": "Lord, teach me to wait in prayer with others. They stayed together in one room, praying, without knowing what would happen. Hold us together, and help me devote myself to prayer when I would rather rush ahead. Amen.", "reflect": "Who could you pray with this week?"}, {"day": 30, "date": "2027-05-10", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "I will pour out my Spirit", "ref": "Joel 2:28-32", "leadIn": "Joel promises that God will pour out his Spirit on all people: sons and daughters, old and young, even servants. Everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved. The church later heard these words fulfilled at Pentecost.", "prayer": "God, pour out your Spirit on your people, and on me. Let old and young, women and men, dream your dreams and see your visions. Do not let me think I am too ordinary for you. Help me call on your name and be saved. Amen.", "reflect": "What would it look like for the Spirit to be poured out on your community?"}, {"day": 31, "date": "2027-05-11", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "Dry bones", "ref": "Ezekiel 37:1-14", "leadIn": "Ezekiel is set down in a valley of dry bones. God asks, can these bones live? As Ezekiel speaks, breath comes into them and they stand. The promise is that God will put his Spirit in his people and they will live.", "prayer": "Breath of God, breathe on what is dry in me. There are bones in my life that I thought were beyond hope. Make them live. Speak your word to what feels dead, and give me the faith to say, you know. Amen.", "reflect": "Where do you feel dry or lifeless? Can you invite God's breath there?"}, {"day": 32, "date": "2027-05-12", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "Rivers of living water", "ref": "John 7:37-39", "leadIn": "On the last day of a festival, Jesus calls out: whoever is thirsty, come to me and drink. Rivers of living water will flow from within. John explains that he was speaking of the Spirit.", "prayer": "Jesus, I am thirsty. Fill me, and let your life flow through me to others. Where I have been drinking from places that do not satisfy, bring me to you. Make me a river and not a pond. Amen.", "reflect": "What are you thirsty for today?"}, {"day": 33, "date": "2027-05-13", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "The Spirit helps us pray", "ref": "Romans 8:22-27", "leadIn": "Creation groans, and we groan with it, waiting for what God has promised. In our weakness, the Spirit prays for us with sighs too deep for words. We do not need to find the perfect prayer.", "prayer": "Spirit of God, pray in me when I have no words. Thank you for helping me in my weakness, and for groaning with me when the world groans. Teach me to hope for what I cannot see, and to wait for it with patience. Amen.", "reflect": "What could you bring to God today without worrying about the right words?"}, {"day": 34, "date": "2027-05-14", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "Fruit of the Spirit", "ref": "Galatians 5:16-25", "leadIn": "Paul contrasts living by the flesh with living by the Spirit. The Spirit's fruit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control. If we live by the Spirit, we should keep in step with the Spirit.", "prayer": "Holy Spirit, grow your fruit in me: love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, self-control. Show me one area where I can keep in step with you today, and help me stop living by my own impulses. Amen.", "reflect": "Which fruit of the Spirit do you most want to grow right now?"}, {"day": 35, "date": "2027-05-15", "week": "Week 7: Waiting for the Spirit", "title": "Send forth your Spirit", "ref": "Psalm 104:24-34", "leadIn": "The psalmist marvels at the sea and all its creatures, which depend on God. When he sends his breath, they are created, and the face of the ground is renewed. The psalm ends with a prayer: may the Lord rejoice in his works.", "prayer": "Lord, you made the earth and the sea and everything in them, and you renew them. Renew me. Send out your Spirit, and let me rejoice in you. Let my meditation be pleasing to you, and teach me to sing while I live. Amen.", "reflect": "Where do you see creation renewed around you?"}, {"day": 36, "date": "2027-05-16", "week": "Pentecost", "title": "The day of Pentecost", "ref": "Acts 2:1-21", "leadIn": "Fifty days after Easter, the disciples are together when a sound like a rushing wind fills the house. Tongues of fire rest on each of them, and they begin to speak in other languages. Peter says this is what Joel promised: God's Spirit poured out on everyone.", "prayer": "Come, Holy Spirit. Fill me and your church with your fire. Let us speak, each in our own way, of your mighty works. Send us out to tell them, and help us listen to each other. Thank you for fifty days of Easter. Amen.", "reflect": "How might you carry the story of Easter into the days ahead?"}], "scripture": {"1": [[1, "“Most certainly, I tell you, one who doesn’t enter by the door into the sheep fold, but climbs up some other way, is a thief and a robber.", true], [2, "But one who enters in by the door is the shepherd of the sheep.", false], [3, "The gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and the sheep listen to his voice. He calls his own sheep by name and leads them out.", false], [4, "Whenever he brings out his own sheep, he goes before them; and the sheep follow him, for they know his voice.", false], [5, "They will by no means follow a stranger, but will flee from him; for they don’t know the voice of strangers.”", false], [6, "Jesus spoke this parable to them, but they didn’t understand what he was telling them.", false], [7, "Jesus therefore said to them again, “Most certainly, I tell you, I am the sheep’s door.", true], [8, "All who came before me are thieves and robbers, but the sheep didn’t listen to them.", false], [9, "I am the door. If anyone enters in by me, he will be saved, and will go in and go out and will find pasture.", false], [10, "The thief only comes to steal, kill, and destroy. I came that they may have life, and may have it abundantly.", false]], "2": [[11, "“I am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep.", true], [12, "He who is a hired hand, and not a shepherd, who doesn’t own the sheep, sees the wolf coming, leaves the sheep, and flees. The wolf snatches the sheep and scatters them.", false], [13, "The hired hand flees because he is a hired hand and doesn’t care for the sheep.", false], [14, "I am the good shepherd. I know my own, and I’m known by my own;", false], [15, "even as the Father knows me, and I know the Father. I lay down my life for the sheep.", false], [16, "I have other sheep which are not of this fold. I must bring them also, and they will hear my voice. They will become one flock with one shepherd.", false], [17, "Therefore the Father loves me, because I lay down my life, that I may take it again.", false], [18, "No one takes it away from me, but I lay it down by myself. I have power to lay it down, and I have power to take it again. I received this commandment from my Father.”", false]], "3": [[22, "It was the Feast of the Dedication at Jerusalem.", true], [23, "It was winter, and Jesus was walking in the temple, in Solomon’s porch.", false], [24, "The Jews therefore came around him and said to him, “How long will you hold us in suspense? If you are the Christ, tell us plainly.”", false], [25, "Jesus answered them, “I told you, and you don’t believe. The works that I do in my Father’s name, these testify about me.", true], [26, "But you don’t believe, because you are not of my sheep, as I told you.", false], [27, "My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me.", false], [28, "I give eternal life to them. They will never perish, and no one will snatch them out of my hand.", false], [29, "My Father who has given them to me is greater than all. No one is able to snatch them out of my Father’s hand.", false], [30, "I and the Father are one.”", false]], "4": [[11, "“‘For the Lord GOD says: “Behold, I myself, even I, will search for my sheep, and will seek them out.", true], [12, "As a shepherd seeks out his flock in the day that he is amongst his sheep that are scattered abroad, so I will seek out my sheep. I will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day.", false], [13, "I will bring them out from the peoples, and gather them from the countries, and will bring them into their own land. I will feed them on the mountains of Israel, by the watercourses, and in all the inhabited places of the country.", false], [14, "I will feed them with good pasture, and their fold will be on the mountains of the height of Israel. There they will lie down in a good fold. They will feed on rich pasture on the mountains of Israel.", false], [15, "I myself will be the shepherd of my sheep, and I will cause them to lie down,” says the Lord GOD.", false], [16, "“I will seek that which was lost, and will bring back that which was driven away, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen that which was sick; but I will destroy the fat and the strong. I will feed them in justice.”’", false]], "5": [[19, "For it is commendable if someone endures pain, suffering unjustly, because of conscience towards God.", true], [20, "For what glory is it if, when you sin, you patiently endure beating? But if when you do well, you patiently endure suffering, this is commendable with God.", false], [21, "For you were called to this, because Christ also suffered for us, leaving you an example, that you should follow his steps,", false], [22, "who didn’t sin, “neither was deceit found in his mouth.”", false], [23, "When he was cursed, he didn’t curse back. When he suffered, he didn’t threaten, but committed himself to him who judges righteously.", false], [24, "He himself bore our sins in his body on the tree, that we, having died to sins, might live to righteousness. You were healed by his wounds.", false], [25, "For you were going astray like sheep; but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls.", false]], "6": [[1, "Oh come, let’s sing to the LORD.\nLet’s shout aloud to the rock of our salvation!", true], [2, "Let’s come before his presence with thanksgiving.\nLet’s extol him with songs!", false], [3, "For the LORD is a great God,\na great King above all gods.", false], [4, "In his hand are the deep places of the earth.\nThe heights of the mountains are also his.", false], [5, "The sea is his, and he made it.\nHis hands formed the dry land.", false], [6, "Oh come, let’s worship and bow down.\nLet’s kneel before the LORD, our Maker,", false], [7, "for he is our God.\nWe are the people of his pasture,\nand the sheep in his care.\nToday, oh that you would hear his voice!", false]], "7": [[9, "After these things I looked, and behold, a great multitude which no man could count, out of every nation and of all tribes, peoples, and languages, standing before the throne and before the Lamb, dressed in white robes, with palm branches in their hands.", true], [10, "They cried with a loud voice, saying, “Salvation be to our God, who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb!”", false], [11, "All the angels were standing around the throne, the elders, and the four living creatures; and they fell on their faces before his throne, and worshipped God,", true], [12, "saying, “Amen! Blessing, glory, wisdom, thanksgiving, honour, power, and might, be to our God forever and ever! Amen.”", false], [13, "One of the elders answered, saying to me, “These who are arrayed in the white robes, who are they, and where did they come from?”", true], [14, "I told him, “My lord, you know.” He said to me, “These are those who came out of the great suffering. They washed their robes and made them white in the Lamb’s blood.", true], [15, "Therefore they are before the throne of God, and they serve him day and night in his temple. He who sits on the throne will spread his tabernacle over them.", true], [16, "They will never be hungry or thirsty any more. The sun won’t beat on them, nor any heat;", false], [17, "for the Lamb who is in the middle of the throne shepherds them and leads them to springs of life-giving waters. And God will wipe away every tear from their eyes.”", false]], "8": [[1, "“I am the true vine, and my Father is the farmer.", true], [2, "Every branch in me that doesn’t bear fruit, he takes away. Every branch that bears fruit, he prunes, that it may bear more fruit.", false], [3, "You are already pruned clean because of the word which I have spoken to you.", false], [4, "Remain in me, and I in you. As the branch can’t bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, so neither can you, unless you remain in me.", false], [5, "I am the vine. You are the branches. He who remains in me and I in him bears much fruit, for apart from me you can do nothing.", false], [6, "If a man doesn’t remain in me, he is thrown out as a branch and is withered; and they gather them, throw them into the fire, and they are burnt.", false], [7, "If you remain in me, and my words remain in you, you will ask whatever you desire, and it will be done for you.", false], [8, "“In this my Father is glorified, that you bear much fruit; and so you will be my disciples.", true]], "9": [[9, "Even as the Father has loved me, I also have loved you. Remain in my love.", true], [10, "If you keep my commandments, you will remain in my love, even as I have kept my Father’s commandments and remain in his love.", false], [11, "I have spoken these things to you, that my joy may remain in you, and that your joy may be made full.", false], [12, "“This is my commandment, that you love one another, even as I have loved you.", true], [13, "Greater love has no one than this, that someone lay down his life for his friends.", false], [14, "You are my friends if you do whatever I command you.", false], [15, "No longer do I call you servants, for the servant doesn’t know what his lord does. But I have called you friends, for everything that I heard from my Father, I have made known to you.", false], [16, "You didn’t choose me, but I chose you and appointed you, that you should go and bear fruit, and that your fruit should remain; that whatever you will ask of the Father in my name, he may give it to you.", false], [17, "“I command these things to you, that you may love one another.", true]], "10": [[1, "“Don’t let your heart be troubled. Believe in God. Believe also in me.", true], [2, "In my Father’s house are many homes. If it weren’t so, I would have told you. I am going to prepare a place for you.", false], [3, "If I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again and will receive you to myself; that where I am, you may be there also.", false], [4, "You know where I go, and you know the way.”", false], [5, "Thomas said to him, “Lord, we don’t know where you are going. How can we know the way?”", true], [6, "Jesus said to him, “I am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father, except through me.", true], [7, "If you had known me, you would have known my Father also. From now on, you know him and have seen him.”", false]], "11": [[15, "If you love me, keep my commandments.", true], [16, "I will pray to the Father, and he will give you another Counsellor, that he may be with you forever:", false], [17, "the Spirit of truth, whom the world can’t receive, for it doesn’t see him and doesn’t know him. You know him, for he lives with you and will be in you.", false], [18, "I will not leave you orphans. I will come to you.", false], [19, "Yet a little while, and the world will see me no more; but you will see me. Because I live, you will live also.", false], [20, "In that day you will know that I am in my Father, and you in me, and I in you.", false], [21, "One who has my commandments and keeps them, that person is one who loves me. One who loves me will be loved by my Father, and I will love him, and will reveal myself to him.”", false]], "12": [[16, "By this we know love, because he laid down his life for us. And we ought to lay down our lives for the brothers.", true], [17, "But whoever has the world’s goods and sees his brother in need, then closes his heart of compassion against him, how does God’s love remain in him?", false], [18, "My little children, let’s not love in word only, or with the tongue only, but in deed and truth.", true], [19, "And by this we know that we are of the truth and persuade our hearts before him,", false], [20, "because if our heart condemns us, God is greater than our heart, and knows all things.", false], [21, "Beloved, if our hearts don’t condemn us, we have boldness towards God;", false], [22, "so whatever we ask, we receive from him, because we keep his commandments and do the things that are pleasing in his sight.", false], [23, "This is his commandment, that we should believe in the name of his Son, Jesus Christ, and love one another, even as he commanded.", false], [24, "He who keeps his commandments remains in him, and he in him. By this we know that he remains in us, by the Spirit which he gave us.", false]], "13": [[6, "Seek the LORD while he may be found.\nCall on him while he is near.", true], [7, "Let the wicked forsake his way,\nand the unrighteous man his thoughts.\nLet him return to the LORD, and he will have mercy on him,\nto our God, for he will freely pardon.", false], [8, "“For my thoughts are not your thoughts,\nand your ways are not my ways,” says the LORD.", true], [9, "“For as the heavens are higher than the earth,\nso are my ways higher than your ways,\nand my thoughts than your thoughts.", false], [10, "For as the rain comes down and the snow from the sky,\nand doesn’t return there, but waters the earth,\nand makes it grow and bud,\nand gives seed to the sower and bread to the eater;", false], [11, "so is my word that goes out of my mouth:\nit will not return to me void,\nbut it will accomplish that which I please,\nand it will prosper in the thing I sent it to do.", false], [12, "For you shall go out with joy,\nand be led out with peace.\nThe mountains and the hills will break out before you into singing;\nand all the trees of the fields will clap their hands.", false], [13, "Instead of the thorn the cypress tree will come up;\nand instead of the brier the myrtle tree will come up.\nIt will make a name for the LORD,\nfor an everlasting sign that will not be cut off.”", false]], "14": [[1, "Blessed is the man who doesn’t walk in the counsel of the wicked,\nnor stand on the path of sinners,\nnor sit in the seat of scoffers;", true], [2, "but his delight is in the LORD’s law.\nOn his law he meditates day and night.", false], [3, "He will be like a tree planted by the streams of water,\nthat produces its fruit in its season,\nwhose leaf also does not wither.\nWhatever he does shall prosper.", false], [4, "The wicked are not so,\nbut are like the chaff which the wind drives away.", false], [5, "Therefore the wicked shall not stand in the judgement,\nnor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.", false], [6, "For the LORD knows the way of the righteous,\nbut the way of the wicked shall perish.", false]], "15": [[1, "Peter and John were going up into the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth hour.", true], [2, "A certain man who was lame from his mother’s womb was being carried, whom they laid daily at the door of the temple which is called Beautiful, to ask gifts for the needy of those who entered into the temple.", false], [3, "Seeing Peter and John about to go into the temple, he asked to receive gifts for the needy.", false], [4, "Peter, fastening his eyes on him, with John, said, “Look at us.”", false], [5, "He listened to them, expecting to receive something from them.", false], [6, "But Peter said, “I have no silver or gold, but what I have, that I give you. In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!”", false], [7, "He took him by the right hand and raised him up. Immediately his feet and his ankle bones received strength.", false], [8, "Leaping up, he stood and began to walk. He entered with them into the temple, walking, leaping, and praising God.", false], [9, "All the people saw him walking and praising God.", false], [10, "They recognised him, that it was he who used to sit begging for gifts for the needy at the Beautiful Gate of the temple. They were filled with wonder and amazement at what had happened to him.", false]], "16": [[32, "The multitude of those who believed were of one heart and soul. Not one of them claimed that anything of the things which he possessed was his own, but they had all things in common.", true], [33, "With great power, the apostles gave their testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus. Great grace was on them all.", false], [34, "For neither was there amongst them any who lacked, for as many as were owners of lands or houses sold them, and brought the proceeds of the things that were sold,", false], [35, "and laid them at the apostles’ feet; and distribution was made to each, according as anyone had need.", false]], "17": [[10, "Now there was a certain disciple at Damascus named Ananias. The Lord said to him in a vision, “Ananias!” He said, “Behold, it’s me, Lord.”", true], [11, "The Lord said to him, “Arise and go to the street which is called Straight, and enquire in the house of Judah for one named Saul, a man of Tarsus. For behold, he is praying,", true], [12, "and in a vision he has seen a man named Ananias coming in and laying his hands on him, that he might receive his sight.”", false], [13, "But Ananias answered, “Lord, I have heard from many about this man, how much evil he did to your saints at Jerusalem.", true], [14, "Here he has authority from the chief priests to bind all who call on your name.”", false], [15, "But the Lord said to him, “Go your way, for he is my chosen vessel to bear my name before the nations and kings, and the children of Israel.", true], [16, "For I will show him how many things he must suffer for my name’s sake.”", false], [17, "Ananias departed and entered into the house. Laying his hands on him, he said, “Brother Saul, the Lord, who appeared to you on the road by which you came, has sent me that you may receive your sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.”", true], [18, "Immediately something like scales fell from his eyes, and he received his sight. He arose and was baptised.", false], [19, "He took food and was strengthened. Saul stayed several days with the disciples who were at Damascus.", false]], "18": [[34, "Peter opened his mouth and said, “Truly I perceive that God doesn’t show favouritism;", true], [35, "but in every nation he who fears him and works righteousness is acceptable to him.", false], [36, "The word which he sent to the children of Israel, preaching good news of peace by Jesus Christ—he is Lord of all—", false], [37, "you yourselves know what happened, which was proclaimed throughout all Judea, beginning from Galilee, after the baptism which John preached;", false], [38, "how God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power, who went about doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, for God was with him.", false], [39, "We are witnesses of everything he did both in the country of the Jews and in Jerusalem; whom they also killed, hanging him on a tree.", false], [40, "God raised him up the third day and gave him to be revealed,", false], [41, "not to all the people, but to witnesses who were chosen before by God, to us, who ate and drank with him after he rose from the dead.", false], [42, "He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that this is he who is appointed by God as the Judge of the living and the dead.", false], [43, "All the prophets testify about him, that through his name everyone who believes in him will receive remission of sins.”", false]], "19": [[1, "That which was from the beginning, that which we have heard, that which we have seen with our eyes, that which we saw, and our hands touched, concerning the Word of life", true], [2, "(and the life was revealed, and we have seen, and testify, and declare to you the life, the eternal life, which was with the Father, and was revealed to us);", false], [3, "that which we have seen and heard we declare to you, that you also may have fellowship with us. Yes, and our fellowship is with the Father and with his Son, Jesus Christ.", false], [4, "And we write these things to you, that our joy may be fulfilled.", false]], "20": [[6, "In this mountain, the LORD of Armies will make all peoples a feast of choice meat, a feast of choice wines, of choice meat full of marrow, of well refined choice wines.", true], [7, "He will destroy in this mountain the surface of the covering that covers all peoples, and the veil that is spread over all nations.", false], [8, "He has swallowed up death forever! The Lord GOD will wipe away tears from off all faces. He will take the reproach of his people away from off all the earth, for the LORD has spoken it.", false], [9, "It shall be said in that day, “Behold, this is our God! We have waited for him, and he will save us! This is the LORD! We have waited for him. We will be glad and rejoice in his salvation!”", true]], "21": [[1, "I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and the first earth have passed away, and the sea is no more.", true], [2, "I saw the holy city, New Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared like a bride adorned for her husband.", false], [3, "I heard a loud voice out of heaven saying, “Behold, God’s dwelling is with people; and he will dwell with them, and they will be his people, and God himself will be with them as their God.", false], [4, "He will wipe away every tear from their eyes. Death will be no more; neither will there be mourning, nor crying, nor pain any more. The first things have passed away.”", false], [5, "He who sits on the throne said, “Behold, I am making all things new.” He said, “Write, for these words of God are faithful and true.”", true], [6, "He said to me, “I am the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End. I will give freely to him who is thirsty from the spring of the water of life.", false], [7, "He who overcomes, I will give him these things. I will be his God, and he will be my son.", false]], "22": [[5, "But now I am going to him who sent me, and none of you asks me, ‘Where are you going?’", true], [6, "But because I have told you these things, sorrow has filled your heart.", false], [7, "Nevertheless I tell you the truth: It is to your advantage that I go away; for if I don’t go away, the Counsellor won’t come to you. But if I go, I will send him to you.", false], [8, "When he has come, he will convict the world about sin, about righteousness, and about judgement;", false], [9, "about sin, because they don’t believe in me;", false], [10, "about righteousness, because I am going to my Father, and you won’t see me any more;", false], [11, "about judgement, because the prince of this world has been judged.", false], [12, "“I still have many things to tell you, but you can’t bear them now.", true], [13, "However, when he, the Spirit of truth, has come, he will guide you into all truth, for he will not speak from himself; but whatever he hears, he will speak. He will declare to you things that are coming.", false], [14, "He will glorify me, for he will take from what is mine and will declare it to you.", false], [15, "All things that the Father has are mine; therefore I said that he takes of mine and will declare it to you.", false]], "23": [[16, "“A little while, and you will not see me. Again a little while, and you will see me.”", true], [17, "Some of his disciples therefore said to one another, “What is this that he says to us, ‘A little while, and you won’t see me, and again a little while, and you will see me;’ and, ‘Because I go to the Father’?”", true], [18, "They said therefore, “What is this that he says, ‘A little while’? We don’t know what he is saying.”", false], [19, "Therefore Jesus perceived that they wanted to ask him, and he said to them, “Do you enquire amongst yourselves concerning this, that I said, ‘A little while, and you won’t see me, and again a little while, and you will see me’?", true], [20, "Most certainly I tell you that you will weep and lament, but the world will rejoice. You will be sorrowful, but your sorrow will be turned into joy.", false], [21, "A woman, when she gives birth, has sorrow because her time has come. But when she has delivered the child, she doesn’t remember the anguish any more, for the joy that a human being is born into the world.", false], [22, "Therefore you now have sorrow, but I will see you again, and your heart will rejoice, and no one will take your joy away from you.", false], [23, "“In that day you will ask me no questions. Most certainly I tell you, whatever you may ask of the Father in my name, he will give it to you.", true], [24, "Until now, you have asked nothing in my name. Ask, and you will receive, that your joy may be made full.", false]], "24": [[1, "Jesus said these things, then lifting up his eyes to heaven, he said, “Father, the time has come. Glorify your Son, that your Son may also glorify you;", true], [2, "even as you gave him authority over all flesh, so he will give eternal life to all whom you have given him.", false], [3, "This is eternal life, that they should know you, the only true God, and him whom you sent, Jesus Christ.", false], [4, "I glorified you on the earth. I have accomplished the work which you have given me to do.", false], [5, "Now, Father, glorify me with your own self with the glory which I had with you before the world existed.", false], [6, "“I revealed your name to the people whom you have given me out of the world. They were yours, and you have given them to me. They have kept your word.", true], [7, "Now they have known that all things whatever you have given me are from you,", false], [8, "for the words which you have given me I have given to them; and they received them, and knew for sure that I came from you. They have believed that you sent me.", false], [9, "I pray for them. I don’t pray for the world, but for those whom you have given me, for they are yours.", false], [10, "All things that are mine are yours, and yours are mine, and I am glorified in them.", false], [11, "I am no more in the world, but these are in the world, and I am coming to you. Holy Father, keep them through your name which you have given me, that they may be one, even as we are.", false]], "25": [[20, "“Not for these only do I pray, but for those also who will believe in me through their word,", true], [21, "that they may all be one; even as you, Father, are in me, and I in you, that they also may be one in us; that the world may believe that you sent me.", false], [22, "The glory which you have given me, I have given to them, that they may be one, even as we are one,", false], [23, "I in them, and you in me, that they may be perfected into one, that the world may know that you sent me and loved them, even as you loved me.", false], [24, "Father, I desire that they also whom you have given me be with me where I am, that they may see my glory which you have given me, for you loved me before the foundation of the world.", false], [25, "Righteous Father, the world hasn’t known you, but I knew you; and these knew that you sent me.", false], [26, "I made known to them your name, and will make it known; that the love with which you loved me may be in them, and I in them.”", false]], "26": [[1, "The first book I wrote, Theophilus, concerned all that Jesus began both to do and to teach,", true], [2, "until the day in which he was received up, after he had given commandment through the Holy Spirit to the apostles whom he had chosen.", false], [3, "To these he also showed himself alive after he suffered, by many proofs, appearing to them over a period of forty days and speaking about God’s Kingdom.", false], [4, "Being assembled together with them, he commanded them, “Don’t depart from Jerusalem, but wait for the promise of the Father, which you heard from me.", false], [5, "For John indeed baptised in water, but you will be baptised in the Holy Spirit not many days from now.”", false], [6, "Therefore, when they had come together, they asked him, “Lord, are you now restoring the kingdom to Israel?”", true], [7, "He said to them, “It isn’t for you to know times or seasons which the Father has set within his own authority.", true], [8, "But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you. You will be witnesses to me in Jerusalem, in all Judea and Samaria, and to the uttermost parts of the earth.”", false], [9, "When he had said these things, as they were looking, he was taken up, and a cloud received him out of their sight.", true], [10, "While they were looking steadfastly into the sky as he went, behold, two men stood by them in white clothing,", false], [11, "who also said, “You men of Galilee, why do you stand looking into the sky? This Jesus, who was received up from you into the sky, will come back in the same way as you saw him going into the sky.”", false]], "27": [[15, "For this cause I also, having heard of the faith in the Lord Jesus which is amongst you and the love which you have towards all the saints,", true], [16, "don’t cease to give thanks for you, making mention of you in my prayers,", false], [17, "that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give to you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him,", false], [18, "having the eyes of your hearts enlightened, that you may know what is the hope of his calling, and what are the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints,", false], [19, "and what is the exceeding greatness of his power towards us who believe, according to that working of the strength of his might", false], [20, "which he worked in Christ when he raised him from the dead and made him to sit at his right hand in the heavenly places,", false], [21, "far above all rule, authority, power, dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this age, but also in that which is to come.", false], [22, "He put all things in subjection under his feet, and gave him to be head over all things for the assembly,", false], [23, "which is his body, the fullness of him who fills all in all.", false]], "28": [[44, "He said to them, “This is what I told you while I was still with you, that all things which are written in the law of Moses, the prophets, and the psalms concerning me must be fulfilled.”", true], [45, "Then he opened their minds, that they might understand the Scriptures.", true], [46, "He said to them, “Thus it is written, and thus it was necessary for the Christ to suffer and to rise from the dead the third day,", false], [47, "and that repentance and remission of sins should be preached in his name to all the nations, beginning at Jerusalem.", false], [48, "You are witnesses of these things.", false], [49, "Behold, I send out the promise of my Father on you. But wait in the city of Jerusalem until you are clothed with power from on high.”", false], [50, "He led them out as far as Bethany, and he lifted up his hands and blessed them.", true], [51, "While he blessed them, he withdrew from them and was carried up into heaven.", false], [52, "They worshipped him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy,", false], [53, "and were continually in the temple, praising and blessing God. Amen.", false]], "29": [[12, "Then they returned to Jerusalem from the mountain called Olivet, which is near Jerusalem, a Sabbath day’s journey away.", true], [13, "When they had come in, they went up into the upper room where they were staying, that is Peter, John, James, Andrew, Philip, Thomas, Bartholomew, Matthew, James the son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas the son of James.", false], [14, "All these with one accord continued steadfastly in prayer and supplication, along with the women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with his brothers.", false]], "30": [[28, "“It will happen afterward, that I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh;\nand your sons and your daughters will prophesy.\nYour old men will dream dreams.\nYour young men will see visions.", true], [29, "And also on the servants and on the handmaids in those days,\nI will pour out my Spirit.", false], [30, "I will show wonders in the heavens and on the earth:\nblood, fire, and pillars of smoke.", false], [31, "The sun will be turned into darkness,\nand the moon into blood,\nbefore the great and terrible day of the LORD comes.", false], [32, "It will happen that whoever will call on the LORD’s name shall be saved;\nfor in Mount Zion and in Jerusalem there will be those who escape,\nas the LORD has said,\nand amongst the remnant, those whom the LORD calls.", false]], "31": [[1, "The LORD’s hand was on me, and he brought me out in the LORD’s Spirit, and set me down in the middle of the valley; and it was full of bones.", true], [2, "He caused me to pass by them all around; and behold, there were very many in the open valley, and behold, they were very dry.", false], [3, "He said to me, “Son of man, can these bones live?” I answered, “Lord GOD, you know.”", false], [4, "Again he said to me, “Prophesy over these bones, and tell them, ‘You dry bones, hear the LORD’s word.", true], [5, "The Lord GOD says to these bones: “Behold, I will cause breath to enter into you, and you will live.", false], [6, "I will lay sinews on you, and will bring up flesh on you, and cover you with skin, and put breath in you, and you will live. Then you will know that I am the LORD.”’”", false], [7, "So I prophesied as I was commanded. As I prophesied, there was a noise, and behold, there was an earthquake. Then the bones came together, bone to its bone.", true], [8, "I saw, and, behold, there were sinews on them, and flesh came up, and skin covered them above; but there was no breath in them.", false], [9, "Then he said to me, “Prophesy to the wind, prophesy, son of man, and tell the wind, ‘The Lord GOD says: “Come from the four winds, breath, and breathe on these slain, that they may live.”’”", true], [10, "So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived, and stood up on their feet, an exceedingly great army.", true], [11, "Then he said to me, “Son of man, these bones are the whole house of Israel. Behold, they say, ‘Our bones are dried up, and our hope is lost. We are completely cut off.’", true], [12, "Therefore prophesy, and tell them, ‘The Lord GOD says: “Behold, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, my people; and I will bring you into the land of Israel.", false], [13, "You will know that I am the LORD, when I have opened your graves and caused you to come up out of your graves, my people.", false], [14, "I will put my Spirit in you, and you will live. Then I will place you in your own land; and you will know that I, the LORD, have spoken it and performed it,” says the LORD.’”", false]], "32": [[37, "Now on the last and greatest day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried out, “If anyone is thirsty, let him come to me and drink!", true], [38, "He who believes in me, as the Scripture has said, from within him will flow rivers of living water.”", false], [39, "But he said this about the Spirit, which those believing in him were to receive. For the Holy Spirit was not yet given, because Jesus wasn’t yet glorified.", false]], "33": [[22, "For we know that the whole creation groans and travails in pain together until now.", true], [23, "Not only so, but ourselves also, who have the first fruits of the Spirit, even we ourselves groan within ourselves, waiting for adoption, the redemption of our body.", false], [24, "For we were saved in hope, but hope that is seen is not hope. For who hopes for that which he sees?", false], [25, "But if we hope for that which we don’t see, we wait for it with patience.", false], [26, "In the same way, the Spirit also helps our weaknesses, for we don’t know how to pray as we ought. But the Spirit himself makes intercession for us with groanings which can’t be uttered.", true], [27, "He who searches the hearts knows what is on the Spirit’s mind, because he makes intercession for the saints according to God.", false]], "34": [[16, "But I say, walk by the Spirit, and you won’t fulfil the lust of the flesh.", true], [17, "For the flesh lusts against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh; and these are contrary to one another, that you may not do the things that you desire.", false], [18, "But if you are led by the Spirit, you are not under the law.", false], [19, "Now the deeds of the flesh are obvious, which are: adultery, sexual immorality, uncleanness, lustfulness,", false], [20, "idolatry, sorcery, hatred, strife, jealousies, outbursts of anger, rivalries, divisions, heresies,", false], [21, "envy, murders, drunkenness, orgies, and things like these; of which I forewarn you, even as I also forewarned you, that those who practise such things will not inherit God’s Kingdom.", false], [22, "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faith,", true], [23, "gentleness, and self-control. Against such things there is no law.", false], [24, "Those who belong to Christ have crucified the flesh with its passions and lusts.", false], [25, "If we live by the Spirit, let’s also walk by the Spirit.", true]], "35": [[24, "LORD, how many are your works!\nIn wisdom, you have made them all.\nThe earth is full of your riches.", true], [25, "There is the sea, great and wide,\nin which are innumerable living things,\nboth small and large animals.", false], [26, "There the ships go,\nand leviathan, whom you formed to play there.", false], [27, "These all wait for you,\nthat you may give them their food in due season.", false], [28, "You give to them; they gather.\nYou open your hand; they are satisfied with good.", false], [29, "You hide your face; they are troubled.\nYou take away their breath; they die and return to the dust.", false], [30, "You send out your Spirit and they are created.\nYou renew the face of the ground.", false], [31, "Let the LORD’s glory endure forever.\nLet the LORD rejoice in his works.", false], [32, "He looks at the earth, and it trembles.\nHe touches the mountains, and they smoke.", false], [33, "I will sing to the LORD as long as I live.\nI will sing praise to my God while I have any being.", false], [34, "Let my meditation be sweet to him.\nI will rejoice in the LORD.", false]], "36": [[1, "Now when the day of Pentecost had come, they were all with one accord in one place.", true], [2, "Suddenly there came from the sky a sound like the rushing of a mighty wind, and it filled all the house where they were sitting.", false], [3, "Tongues like fire appeared and were distributed to them, and one sat on each of them.", false], [4, "They were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak with other languages, as the Spirit gave them the ability to speak.", false], [5, "Now there were dwelling in Jerusalem Jews, devout men, from every nation under the sky.", true], [6, "When this sound was heard, the multitude came together and were bewildered, because everyone heard them speaking in his own language.", false], [7, "They were all amazed and marvelled, saying to one another, “Behold, aren’t all these who speak Galileans?", false], [8, "How do we hear, everyone in our own native language?", false], [9, "Parthians, Medes, Elamites, and people from Mesopotamia, Judea, Cappadocia, Pontus, Asia,", false], [10, "Phrygia, Pamphylia, Egypt, the parts of Libya around Cyrene, visitors from Rome, both Jews and proselytes,", false], [11, "Cretans and Arabians—we hear them speaking in our languages the mighty works of God!”", false], [12, "They were all amazed and were perplexed, saying to one another, “What does this mean?”", false], [13, "Others, mocking, said, “They are filled with new wine.”", false], [14, "But Peter, standing up with the eleven, lifted up his voice and spoke out to them, “You men of Judea and all you who dwell at Jerusalem, let this be known to you, and listen to my words.", true], [15, "For these aren’t drunken, as you suppose, seeing it is only the third hour of the day.", false], [16, "But this is what has been spoken through the prophet Joel:", false], [17, "‘It will be in the last days, says God,\nthat I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh.\nYour sons and your daughters will prophesy.\nYour young men will see visions.\nYour old men will dream dreams.", false], [18, "Yes, and on my servants and on my handmaidens in those days,\nI will pour out my Spirit, and they will prophesy.", false], [19, "I will show wonders in the sky above,\nand signs on the earth beneath:\nblood, and fire, and billows of smoke.", false], [20, "The sun will be turned into darkness,\nand the moon into blood,\nbefore the great and glorious day of the Lord comes.", false], [21, "It will be that whoever will call on the name of the Lord will be saved.’", false]]}};
